-- adequacy finds reach where a law passes it to a function, whatever the law calls its variables; at
-- size 0 the recursive rule never applies, so its mutants die only at size 1, where direct is false
set Node = A | B | C
under test: reach, edge
fact edge(A, B)
fact edge(B, C)
rule one: edge(x, y) => reach(x, y)
rule more: edge(x, y), reach(y, z) => reach(x, z)
law sound: all x: Node, y: Node. holds(reach, x, y) == No || reaches(x, y) == Yes by exhaustion
law sound_uv: all u: Node, v: Node. holds(reach, u, v) == No || reaches(u, v) == Yes by exhaustion
law direct: all x: Node, y: Node, holds(reach, x, y) = Yes. holds(edge, x, y) = Yes by exhaustion size 0
law adequate: mutants of reach by exhaustion size 0. sound
law adequate_uv: mutants of reach by exhaustion size 0. sound_uv
law adequate_direct: mutants of reach by exhaustion size 0. direct
